1. test_yoy_change_basic (Unit test)

GIVEN series 1 has values for the same month in consecutive years (e.g., 2023-01=100, 2024-01=120)
WHEN yoy_change(session, 1, 2024-01) is computed
THEN YoY is returned as a percentage (e.g., 20.0 for +20%).

2. test_yoy_change_no_previous_year (Unit test)

GIVEN the current month exists but the previous-year month is missing
WHEN yoy_change is called
THEN returns None (no comparable baseline).

3. test_yoy_change_previous_year_zero (Unit test)

GIVEN previous-year value is 0 (division unsafe)
WHEN yoy_change is called
THEN returns None to avoid invalid growth output.

4. test_yoy_change_current_value_missing (Unit test)

GIVEN the current month value is NULL
WHEN yoy_change is called
THEN returns None.

5. test_yoy_change_previous_year_missing (Unit test)

GIVEN the previous-year month value is NULL
WHEN yoy_change is called
THEN returns None.

6. test_moving_average_basic (Unit test)

GIVEN a simple series (e.g., 10, 20, 30)
WHEN moving_average(session, id, window=2) is computed
THEN returns a rolling mean series with the first point None and subsequent means correct.

7. test_moving_average_window_one (Unit test)

GIVEN any non-empty series
WHEN window=1 is used
THEN the output aligns with the series values (subject to the “first point None” convention).

8. test_moving_average_handles_missing_values (Unit test)

GIVEN missing values inside the series (e.g., 10, NULL, 30)
WHEN moving average is computed
THEN missing values are ignored when calculating the rolling mean.

9. test_moving_average_empty_series (Unit test)

GIVEN no observations exist for a series
WHEN moving_average is called
THEN returns an empty list.

10. test_missing_rate_basic (Unit test)

GIVEN a range containing both valid and NULL observations
WHEN missing_rate(session, id, start, end) is computed
THEN returns the correct missing proportion (e.g., 1/4 = 0.25).

11. test_missing_rate_all_missing (Unit test)

GIVEN all observations in the range are NULL
WHEN missing_rate is computed
THEN returns 1.0.

12. test_missing_rate_empty_range (Unit test)

GIVEN no observations exist in the requested date range
WHEN missing_rate is computed
THEN returns the defined neutral result (e.g., 0.0) without error.

13. test_analysis_functions_do_not_modify_database (Unit test)

GIVEN an existing set of observations
WHEN analysis functions are called
THEN the database contents remain unchanged (read-only guarantee; no side-effects).

14. test_integration_yoy_and_moving_average_with_file_db (Integration test)

GIVEN a file-based SQLite database populated and then reopened in a new session
WHEN yoy_change and moving_average are executed
THEN results remain correct across sessions, validating ORM mapping + persistence.

B. Series hierarchy queries & classmethod entry points (6 tests)
15. test_seriesmaster_get_children_returns_all_children (Unit test)

GIVEN a Region node with multiple Market children
WHEN SeriesMaster.get_children(session, parent_id) is called
THEN all direct children are returned.

16. test_seriesmaster_get_children_is_ordered_by_name (Unit test)

GIVEN children with unsorted names
WHEN get_children is called
THEN results are ordered lexicographically by name.

17. test_seriesmaster_get_children_empty_when_no_children (Unit test)

GIVEN a node with no children
WHEN get_children is called
THEN returns an empty list.

18. test_seriesmaster_get_by_level_filters_correctly (Unit test)

GIVEN mixed level values (Total/Region/Market), and the environment may contain pre-seeded rows
WHEN SeriesMaster.get_by_level(session, "region") is called
THEN the result set contains the expected region(s) and all returned rows have level == "region".

19. test_seriesmaster_get_by_level_is_ordered_by_name (Unit test)

GIVEN multiple series in the same level
WHEN get_by_level is called
THEN results are ordered by name.

20. test_observation_classmethods_match_analysis_functions (Unit test)

GIVEN a minimal dataset for a market with two years of observations
WHEN calling Observation.yoy_change(...) and Observation.moving_average(...)
THEN classmethod wrappers return correct analytical outputs, demonstrating that ORM classes expose domain behaviour as required.
